#!/usr/bin/env bash
# ^^^ for syntax checking in the editor only

##
## AgentsContext.FrontForward.include -- the tool files in front of the operations they own under their new names (F1.4 of the refactorings epic, first stage).
## Sourced, never run. Functions and one declaration only.
##
## The table below is one line a new name: the entry function of the tool file that owns it, the name, and the operation or operations it goes on under, a
## `--member-*` and a `--magic-*` of one function sharing one new name. A tool file asks AgentsToolsFrontKnows before anything else; for a name it owns, it calls
## AgentsToolsFrontForward, which makes the call again as DistroAgentsTools.fn.sh, under the old name, with every check and gate that call has always had.
## Nothing else of the old operation changes in this stage. The old names are deleted in the last stage, when the operations move out of DistroAgentsTools.fn.sh.
##

